# graphify-out/ is a generated bundle, not source. CI rebuilds it on every push
# to main and publishes it as an artifact; clones fetch it with
#
# Deliberately default-deny — ignore the directory's contents and re-include only
# the hand-written README. Two reasons it is an ignore-all rather than the former
# enumerated list: graph.json is ~53 MB against GitHub's 50 MB per-file push limit
# (zero bypass actors), so no `git add graphify-out` may ever stage it; and a
# future graphify release that emits a new output file then inherits the ignore
# instead of being committed by accident, which is how the 42 MB graph.json got
# tracked in the first place.
#
# NOTE: the trailing `/*` is load-bearing. With a bare `graphify-out/` git does
# not descend into the directory at all, so the negation below would never be
# evaluated and README.md would be ignored too.
graphify-out/*
!graphify-out/README.md

# impeccable design-detector runtime state. The shared `.impeccable/config.json` IS
# tracked (it is the reviewable home for any detector ignore); the dedup cache and the
# per-developer override are machine-local. `**/` because the hook writes a cache
# beside whichever package it scanned, not only at the repo root.
**/.impeccable/hook.cache.json
**/.impeccable/config.local.json

# Tri-Harness Concord Bridge worktrees and audit traces
.worktrees/
.agent-bus/
